{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deterministic agent guardrails deterministic agent guardrails","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md","fileName":"Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deterministic Agent Guardrails","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deterministic agent guardrails deterministic agent guardrails","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md","fileName":"Deterministic Agent Guardrails.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deterministic Agent Guardrails","heading":"Deterministic Agent Guardrails","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Deterministic agent guardrails wrap probabilistic reasoning in enforceable checks. They include schema validation, action allowlists, least-privilege tools, relevance filtering, secret and personal-data filtering, risk thresholds, and human review before code, deployment, or security policy changes.\n\nThe guardrail code—not the agent's confidence—decides whether a workflow passes, fails, falls back, or asks for review. This makes policy behavior testable and ensures that a fluent but malformed or overreaching response cannot silently become an operational action.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"propert